-- title:
--   Encoding blocks of Gaussian integers into the Fermat ring
-- statement:
--   Let $U$ be a list of $N\cdot r$ Gaussian integers with coordinates of absolute value $<2^P$ ($P,r\ge1$), stored on stack `GU`, and let the registers hold $2^P$, $r$, $2^{2rP}$, $2^{4rP}+1$ and $N$. For bounds $Q\ge P$ with $\mathrm{zsz}(r)\le Q$ and $W\ge 4rP+1$, $W \ge \mathrm{zsz}(N)$, the program `encL` consumes $U$ and pushes on `XD` the list of residues `encRes P r blk` (Kronecker packing of each block of $r$ consecutive entries, real parts in the low half and imaginary parts times $2^{2rP}$, reduced modulo $2^{4rP}+1$) for the $N$ blocks of $U$, within cost `encCost N r P Q W`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The machine layer: `IState HS` is a state with $64$ stacks of items (`Item` = integer or mark), an input position and an output; `RM` programs (straight-line register code `RS`, loops `rep`, conditionals, calls of the multiplication procedure through a `MulSpec` $M$ giving its domain and cost) have a functional semantics `p.run s`, a definedness predicate `p.ok M s` and a cost `p.cost M s`; `Spec M p s s' c` abbreviates `p.ok M s ∧ p.run s = s' ∧ p.cost M s ≤ c`. `ints L` / `gints U` push an integer list / a list of pairs as items (head = top); `zsz z` is the bit length of $|z|$. `MulBnd M m Φ` says the multiplication procedure accepts all pairs of integers of bit length $\le m$ at cost $\le Φ$. Register names (`GU`, `CR`, `KB`, `XN`, …) are fixed stack indices.
-- source:
--   D. Harvey, J. van der Hoeven, Integer multiplication in time O(n log n), Ann. of Math. 193 (2021), 563–617 (Theorem 1.1: multitape Turing machine multiplication in O(n log n)). Lemma `NLogN.FW.encL_spec` of the Lean development NLogN/HFW6.lean (lines 58–119), written for the prove2.me integer-multiplication campaign.

